It may not solve your problem with LOO, but I'd recommend sampling for
more than 1000 iterations. It can take a large number of samples to
get DIC/WAIC/etc to converge to a stable value.

Ed

On 7/25/19, Mauricio Garnier-Villarreal <mauga...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Glad that worked.
>
> I dont know what could lead to this behavior, would have to check in more
> detail the data set.
>
> This means that DIC is agreeing with npar about the estimated information,
> while LOO is saying that more information is estimated. Also, this would be
>
> less of an issue with bigger models, which woulkd lead to less likely
> situations with negative "degrees of freedom"
>
>
>
